:: OC Aran Intro [nobr]

/* Written by: Oryan */
/* Intro */
You push open the double doors to the cafeteria, the aroma of lukewarm Salisbury steak and something vaguely fruity assaults your nostrils. The cacophony of pre-teen chatter and the clatter of trays wash over you as you scan the room for a place to sit and spot <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span>’s bright red hair amidst the crowd. He’s sitting at a table near the window next to a boy you vaguely recognize from around the school. You’ve definitely seen him around but can’t quite place him, his name dancing on the tip of your tongue but still just out of reach. <br>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "OC Nikolai",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Uniform",
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "OC Aran",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Uniform",
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

As far as you can recall, he was one of those kids that only interact with a select few, you remember a few times seeing him around <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>, but he never appeared to be one of his lackeys, and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span>, as you can see in this very moment. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:Yellow">Intrigued, and a little apprehensive, you approach the table.</span> As you get closer you take note of a few details, like his dark and almost gothic shade of grey-black hair, a stark contrast to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span>’s bright red, falling across his forehead in a curtain that seems perpetually on the verge of obscuring his eyes as if he'd styled it himself with reckless abandon. Then there’s his eyes, a startling, vibrant blue, a stark contrast to the somberness of his hair and the almost permanent frown etched on his face. He just looks gloomy, but there's something about the way his eyes dart around, absorbing everything, that suggests a deep well of curiosity beneath the surface. <br>
<br>
You reach the table, and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span> grins up at you, his grey eyes sparkling. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Hey! Perfect timing. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span>, this is my friend, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>, this is <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran Keiton</span>."</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> looks up, his blue eyes meeting yours for a brief, intense moment before flickering away. He offers a curt nod, his expression remaining unchanged. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Hello,"</span> he murmurs, his voice surprisingly soft with a hint of a British accent. You manage a smile as you offer him a greeting. <br>
<br>
You can't help but notice his attire. His clothes are clean, clearly expensive, but they have a distinctly disheveled look. A loose-fitting dress shirt hangs precariously off one shoulder, revealing a sliver of pale skin. And then there are the shorts. They’re… exceptionally short. Like, almost scandalously short for this school. To top it all off, he's sporting a pair of large, black earrings and a thick black dog collar around his neck. You’re pretty sure the collar is a blatant violation of the school's dress code, but no one seems to have noticed, or perhaps they simply don't dare to say anything. <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Sit down">>
    You pull out a chair, settling in beside <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span> and asking what they are talking about. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "OC Nikolai",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "OC Aran",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span> shows an air of excitement as he tells you <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> was just telling me about his garden! He grows roses! All different kinds!"</span> causing <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> to actually shift in his seat  <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“And other things, it’s nothing special,”</span> he mumbles, picking at a stray thread on his shirt <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Just a hobby.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“A hobby?"</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span> scoffs playfully. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“He showed me pictures! It's like a secret world back there. You should see it. It's amazing!"</span> <br>
    <br>
    You turn your attention back to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span>, intrigued. Asking him about the garden and what kind of flowers <br>
    <br>
    He hesitates for a moment, then seems to relax slightly, his eyes lighting up with a flicker of genuine interest. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“All sorts,"</span> he says, his voice gaining a little more confidence. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Hybrid teas, floribundas, climbers… I even have a few rare varieties that I imported from France."</span>

    <<if $Player.Traits.includes("Green Thumb")>>
        You’re genuinely impressed, you recognize the dedication and knowledge required to cultivate rare roses. <br>
        <br>
    <<else>>
        you’re not sure if you should be impressed, you know nothing about gardening and those names mean nothing to you <br>
        <br>
    <</if>>

    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span> throws an arm around <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span>'s shoulder, giving him a playful shake. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Don't let him fool you. He's a total softie. Underneath all that gloom, he's a big old flower enthusiast."</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> shoves <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span>'s arm off, a little harder than necessary. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Don't be ridiculous,"</span> he mutters, his cheeks flushing again. He pointedly avoids your gaze. You suppress a grin. It's clear that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span>, despite his attempts at indifference, is enjoying the attention. You glance at his tray, <span style="color:LightCoral">noticing it's practically untouched save for a small apple.</span> <br>
    <br>
    You brush the thought away and instead inquire as to how long he’s been going to Preston. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Since grade 2,"</span> he replies, still fiddling with the thread on his shirt. You jokingly call him a veteran compared to you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span> to which <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> simply responds with a shrug followed by an awkward silence. <br>
    <br>
    The silence stretches for a moment. Until You decide to break the tension by talking about anything and settling on the topic of your family which leads to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> plainly telling you his expression returning to its usual somberness. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“My parents are in the UK. I have staff who take care of me."</span> You try not to let your surprise show. You know Preston was a school for wealthy kids, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span>'s situation seems… extra unusual. Before you can comment on it, he shrugs and adds <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“at least I’ve got my kid brother”</span> with the unmistakable emergence of a smirk. <br>
    <br>
    The conversation goes an as such with little focus on any giving topic, at one moment a comment about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span>’s attire leads to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span> chiming in with a <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Tell me about it, you should see the looks I get for my hair."</span>
    To which <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> replies with a swift "Your hair is glorious," with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> reaching out and gently twirling a strand of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span>'s red hair around his finger in an almost flirtatious way. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Don't ever cut it."</span> A faint blush crept up <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Niki</span>'s neck. You couldn't help but notice the easy familiarity between them, a connection that seemed to have formed almost instantly. <br>
    <br>
    As the lunch bell rang, signaling the end of the break, you stood up, Telling <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> how nice it was to meet him. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“The pleasure was mutual,"</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Aran</span> replied, a hint of a smile playing on his lips. He stood up, as he walked away, the black dog collar glinted in the light, you are left with a mix of curiosity and apprehension. <br>
